# ENT-14 — Load Test Scale Projection

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/load-test-scale-projection-governance.md`.

- The projection extrapolates the ENT-13 5-branch measured baseline to the
  20-branch target and national tiers. It is **analysis-only**: it never
  activates replica read routing or multi-node traffic and never changes
  production topology.
- The projection is driven by `scripts/load-test-scale-projection.sh` →
  `loadtest:scale-projection-run` (guarded, non-production, read-only). Every
  projected number is labeled modeled/estimated — never a measured production
  benchmark.
- Tiers are monotonic-increasing (5 / 10 / 20 / 50 cabang), the lowest tier
  matches the baseline, and higher tiers tie to the shipped LB-1 (horizontal
  scale) and REPLICA-1 (read routing) readiness foundations.
- Bottlenecks are classified against db/cache/queue/php/network/frontend/storage.
- Evidence pack is non-sensitive (tiers + modeled counts + risks + next actions
  — never PII).
- Any new tier / scale-factor / mitigation change must extend
  `config/load_test_scale_projection.php` + tests and stay green under:
  `php artisan foundation:load-test-scale-projection-check --strict`.
- Preserve ENT-5..13: this gate re-verifies queue-retry, idempotency/outbox,
  developer-console, health-check, security-compliance, CI/CD gate,
  deploy/rollback, backup/DR, and load-test-baseline governance.
